# Key EDA Insights Surfaced

- Suicidal ideation and gender gap
  - 3.6 million Canadians experienced suicidal ideation in 2019
  - Women have higher ideation counts, but consult professionals at vastly higher rates: ~3M women consulted vs. ~1M men
  - Men’s consultation rate barely equals their ideation count; women’s exceeds female ideation by over 1 million
  - This absolute headcount gap directly contextualizes why male suicidal mortality is roughly 3x higher than female
- Mental health by income: lower-income bands report lower mental health issues than middle class (noted as a notable and somewhat counterintuitive finding)
- Regional stress: Ontario accounts for over 60% of Canadians coping with daily demands; Atlantic provinces show lower coping percentages
- Data quality signal: CI widths of 0-10 percentage points indicate a small confidence interval, suggesting the data is statistically reliable
- Women consult at 1.5x the rate relative to ideation; men consult at roughly 1x
- Younger people more vulnerable to suicidal thoughts; women more anxiety-prone; men described as more self-reliant (less likely to seek help)
